Key Financial & Tax Considerations (2026) 
• Federal estate tax exemption for 2026: $15,000,000 — Carina's $1.2M estate is well 
below threshold; no federal estate tax concern at this time. 
• Annual gift tax exclusion: $19,000 per recipient — relevant if Carina pursues charitable 
gifting consistent with her Legacy Goals investment objective. 
• ROTH IRA ($220,000): tax-free growth and withdrawals; no required minimum 
distributions during lifetime — highly favorable for legacy planning. 
• Traditional IRA ($480,000): tax-deferred; beneficiaries will owe ordinary income tax on 
distributions — consider naming a trust as beneficiary with proper Conduit or 
Accumulation trust language. 
• Concentrated Acme Technologies stock (~$85,000): unrealized gains may trigger capital 
gains tax upon sale — coordinate with PFA to harvest losses elsewhere and diversify 
over time. 
• Taxable brokerage ($500,000): eligible for stepped-up cost basis at death — 
beneficiaries may inherit with reduced tax burden. 
• ESG preference: document ESG investment mandate in will/trust to guide trustee 
investment decisions post-death. 
 
